      "AI-powered booking app connecting home service providers with clients for plumbing, cleaning, lawn care, and moving.",
      "Speech-to-text booking via Bumi AI for fast, hands-free appointment requests, cancellations, and rescheduling.",
      "Real-time provider status updates and an interactive route map for tracking bookings.",
    ]}
    linkToCode="https://github.com/Bumi-Wipe-Right/frontend"
    linkToLiveSite="https://wiperight.netlify.app/"
    loadingtype="lazy"
    readmeLink="https://github.com/Bumi-Wipe-Right/frontend/blob/main/README.md"
  />


  <Project
    youtube="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QVup5CZ9Y9E"
    youtubePoster="/images/homeward-tails-poster.png"
    vidTitles="Video of the Homeward Tails website"
    projectTitle="Homeward Tails"
    projectLanguages=" Next.js 15, React, Next-Auth, JavaScript, Tailwindcss, CSS, HTML5, MongoDB, Mongoose, Cloudinary, Node Mailer, SendGrid, SWR"
    outcomeLine="Backed by a 438-test suite (269 unit/API/component, 169 E2E)."
    descriptionBullets={[
      "Pet-naming and bio platform helping shelter staff and adoption counselors create impactful, unique adoption bios.",
      "Users search and filter community-submitted names and bios, then sign up to save favorites, follow other users, and submit their own.",
    ]}
    linkToCode="https://github.com/ghiblimagic/PetProfileTailor"
    linkToLiveSite="https://www.homewardtails.com/"
    loadingtype="lazy"
    readmeLink="https://github.com/ghiblimagic/PetProfileTailor/blob/main/README.md"
    decisionLogLink="/blog/homeward-tails-coding-decisions"
  />

  
    <Project
    imgsrc="/images/website-builder.webp"
    vidTitles="Screenshot of the Website Builder Finder guide"
    projectTitle="Website Builder Finder"
    projectLanguages="Next.js, React, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, PostHog"
    projectDescription={`An interactive guide to help with one of the most painful parts of building a website yourself: choosing a website builder. Lets users filter through 15 popular options to find the right fit for their needs.`}
    linkToLiveSite="https://guide.janetspellman.com/"
    loadingtype="lazy"
  />

  <Project
    webmsrc="images/ufancy.webm"
    mp4src="images/ufancy.mp4"
    vidTitles="Video of a responsive wordpress site"
    projectTitle="Ufancy Photobooth"
    projectLanguages="Digital Ocean, linux-based Virtual Machine/Droplet, Ubuntu Server, mySQL, MySQL tuner, WordPress Plugins (Elementor, Contact Form 7, Autocomplete Location Field Contact Form 7, All in One Seo, Flamingo, Optimole, Independent Analytics, OMGF, POST SMTP, Royal Elementor Addons, updraft Plus, w3 Total Cache, Wordfence Security, WP fail2ban, Wp fail2ban blocklist, WP rollback, Wp-sweep), CSS, HTML, Figma"
    projectDescription={`A WordPress site for a client's photobooth business hosted with Digital Ocean.
      
      Boosted performance of this budget-friendly Digital Ocean server without increasing costs, by reducing memory usage 14% via MySQL configuration optimizations, trimming binlog retention, and adding swap space.
      
      Created to capture leads, build their digital business presence, and act as a virtual business card.`}
    linkToCode=""
    linkToLiveSite="https://ufancyphotobooth.com/"
    loadingtype="lazy"
  />

  

  <Project
    webmsrc="images/nourishedByKeto.webm"
    mp4src="images/nourishedByKeto.mp4"
    vidTitles="Video of a responsive blog site"
    projectTitle="Nourished by Keto"
    projectLanguages=" Gatsby.js, Netlify CMS/Decap CMS, React, JavaScript, Tailwindcss, CSS, HTML5,gatsby-plugin-disqus, postcss, daisyui, headlessui"
    projectDescription="A personal blog site for a client; the main theme is how their food choices have affected their health. Their blog posts are integrated with netlify's cms, so the client can add, edit and delete blog post by signing in."
    linkToCode="https://github.com/ghiblimagic/jillyannesite"
    linkToLiveSite="https://nourishedbyketo.netlify.app/"
    loadingtype="lazy"
  />
</div>

<div class="flex align-middle justify-center mt-16 fade-in">
  <GradientButton
    text="Other Projects"
    link="/otherprojects"
    primary
  />
</div>

<style>
  .project-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(1, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 28px;
    max-width: 1280px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  @media (min-width: 1024px) {
    .project-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
  }

  @media (min-width: 1280px) {
    .project-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
  }
</style>